Until then though, all I know for sure is that “this too shall pass” just like so many other things have before.

It’s hard to describe this feeling… It comes on suddenly and without warning – a wave of emotion crashing over you in an instant, leaving you gasping for breath as it passes through your body like lightning striking the ground beneath feet. The first time I experienced something similar happened when out running errands one day; there was no trigger or warning signs leading up to that moment but suddenly everything changed – my heart rate increased dramatically while tears began streaming down cheeks uncontrollably despite how much effort went into trying not too show any emotion whatsoever.
I’m sure many others have felt something similar before whether they realize it or not;

